cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you reference MARGPA Runtime LLM in research or evaluation, please cite
  this software and identify the exact version, commit, or archive used.
title: MARGPA Runtime LLM
type: software
authors:
  - name: Nazuna Research
version: 0.0.0
repository-code: https://github.com/margpa-labs/margpa-runtime-llm
url: https://github.com/margpa-labs/margpa-runtime-llm
abstract: >-
  MARGPA Runtime LLM is a model-independent research prototype that places a
  modular runtime governance control plane around pretrained language models.
  It is designed to separate models, inference backends, configuration,
  governance definitions, guardrails, judges, repair, retrieval, agents,
  storage, user interfaces, and deployment profiles so that components can be
  replaced, disabled, observed, enforced, and compared independently.
keywords:
  - runtime governance
  - language model
  - LLM
  - AI governance
  - modular architecture
  - auditability
  - local inference
